    "resources": "Cheap borrowed geometry admission before Python ownership copy;full contour planning off GIL/creator.Native mask row extrema bounded by4*height;geometry/hull staging charged before allocation.Projection bounded by existing64Mi-work ceiling and cancellable;oversized hull work refuses rather than becoming unbounded.No new memory/RSS claim.",
    "metadata": "Generic width/opaque attributes retained;typed point data requires explicit discard and Undo restores it.Fit ignores stroke glyph footprints;pixels/calibration untouched.",
    "v4": "Only explicit NativePathV4 replacement newly accepts validated three-point rotated_rectangle candidates.Default/V1-V3 remain strict;no record schema/public struct layout change.Older readers can refuse new candidate.Replay restores resolved geometry,not fit intent.",
    "worker": "Reuse captured startControlled lane,source/owner/XY-TCZ/cap/recording guards and retained capture lease through terminal cleanup.Success status staged before commit.Full processing-cap phase reservation remains conservative.",
    "commercial": "Owned projection/hull adapters and original development-only observer.No new runtime library,asset or imported third-party source."
